  "title": "Why is the sea salty? 🌊🧂",
  "hook": "Why is the sea salty, if the rivers that flow into it are fresh water?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_hook",
      "narration": "Why is the sea salty, if the rivers that flow into it are fresh water?",
      "on_screen_text": "Why is the sea salty?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "salty?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_rain",
      "narration": "It all starts with rain: it picks up a tiny bit of acid from the air and slowly wears down rocks.",
      "on_screen_text": "Rain wears down rocks",
      "highlight_words": [
        "rocks"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_rocks",
      "narration": "That frees tiny minerals, like sodium and chlorine, which the water carries away.",
      "on_screen_text": "Sodium and chlorine set loose",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Sodium",
        "chlorine"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_rivers",
      "narration": "Rivers carry them to the sea, but in such small amounts that we can't taste them.",
      "on_screen_text": "Rivers carry them to sea",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Rivers"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_evap",
      "narration": "In the sea, the sun evaporates the water, but the salt doesn't leave: it stays behind.",
      "on_screen_text": "Water leaves, salt stays",
      "highlight_words": [
        "salt"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_cycle",
      "narration": "And so, cycle after cycle for millions of years, the salt kept building up.",
      "on_screen_text": "Millions of years adding up",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Millions"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_vents",
      "narration": "Minerals also pour out of volcanoes and hot springs on the seafloor.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hot springs on the seafloor",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Hot"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_glass",
      "narration": "Today, every liter of seawater holds about thirty-five grams of salt.",
      "on_screen_text": "35 grams per liter",
      "highlight_words": [
        "35"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sal_layer",
      "narration": "If we pulled out all that salt and spread it over the continents, it would make a layer more than a hundred and fifty meters thick.",
      "on_screen_text": "A 150-meter layer!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "150-meter"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
