  "description": "Rain, slightly acidic, wears down rocks and frees minerals that rivers carry to the sea in amounts too small to taste. In the sea the water evaporates but the salt stays, so it built up over millions of years; hydrothermal vents add minerals too. Today every liter holds about 35 g of salt. Original 3D animation.",
